[[:db/retract 17592186083772 :question/answer-fields 17592186081563] {:db/id 17592186083302 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e7f022af-185f-5ff9-8180-e7c6bb598640"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e7f022af-185f-5ff9-8180-e7c6bb598640" :question/id #uuid "e7f022af-185f-5ff9-8180-e7c6bb598640" :question/math-academy-id "q-82640" :question/problem "The length of the curve $y={cos}^{2}⁡x$ on $[0,\\pi ]$ is given by" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)={cos}^{2}⁡x,$ $a=0,$ and $b=\\pi .$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b9178dda-3c7f-55ff-93f7-642762e083ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b9178dda-3c7f-55ff-93f7-642762e083ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9178dda-3c7f-55ff-93f7-642762e083ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e80d767-11f6-5557-956d-f161a62d1488" :answer-field/choices ["answer-385be674-f982-5b0d-a246-7c05ff2eae39" "answer-d8b57b3f-c7b4-5a3a-a497-6401eb5b176f" "answer-b5a976e6-bf11-50a3-a22a-0fbafda71f76" "answer-628f8af6-109d-5b4d-ba07-98c8c66ae500" "answer-4e80d767-11f6-5557-956d-f161a62d1488"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-385be674-f982-5b0d-a246-7c05ff2eae39" :answer/id #uuid "385be674-f982-5b0d-a246-7c05ff2eae39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8b57b3f-c7b4-5a3a-a497-6401eb5b176f" :answer/id #uuid "d8b57b3f-c7b4-5a3a-a497-6401eb5b176f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5a976e6-bf11-50a3-a22a-0fbafda71f76" :answer/id #uuid "b5a976e6-bf11-50a3-a22a-0fbafda71f76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-628f8af6-109d-5b4d-ba07-98c8c66ae500" :answer/id #uuid "628f8af6-109d-5b4d-ba07-98c8c66ae500" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e80d767-11f6-5557-956d-f161a62d1488" :answer/id #uuid "4e80d767-11f6-5557-956d-f161a62d1488" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083205 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6cce7317-466a-565b-96aa-fdea6ef81a13" "question-b4cc4c19-d62f-5fe8-890e-23b350c71bdb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6cce7317-466a-565b-96aa-fdea6ef81a13" :question/id #uuid "6cce7317-466a-565b-96aa-fdea6ef81a13" :question/math-academy-id "q-85595" :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}{x}^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [0,4].$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between two points where $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula:\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}{x}^{3/2},$ $a=0,$ and $b=4.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\sqrt{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=\\sqrt{2x}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{1+[\\sqrt{2x}]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe evaluate this integral using the substitution $u=1+2x.$ Then, $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.$\n\nWe also need to compute new limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 4 \\\\ u & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}]|}_{1}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({9}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27-1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4f3f0bc6-2b44-5994-b979-b5f7080dc894"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4f3f0bc6-2b44-5994-b979-b5f7080dc894" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f3f0bc6-2b44-5994-b979-b5f7080dc894" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3282f6dd-ea0d-5250-b6a0-e1760944dcbc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0ec2b73-e05f-5a1d-a896-08fa4c87c85a" "answer-fa7cfda3-585f-5143-8a02-9cd0f064fb95" "answer-4c99b7f5-f882-59fc-acc5-121343a55257" "answer-b82a6116-d805-5f63-89ef-e785b5a2ca78" "answer-3282f6dd-ea0d-5250-b6a0-e1760944dcbc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0ec2b73-e05f-5a1d-a896-08fa4c87c85a" :answer/id #uuid "f0ec2b73-e05f-5a1d-a896-08fa4c87c85a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa7cfda3-585f-5143-8a02-9cd0f064fb95" :answer/id #uuid "fa7cfda3-585f-5143-8a02-9cd0f064fb95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c99b7f5-f882-59fc-acc5-121343a55257" :answer/id #uuid "4c99b7f5-f882-59fc-acc5-121343a55257" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b82a6116-d805-5f63-89ef-e785b5a2ca78" :answer/id #uuid "b82a6116-d805-5f63-89ef-e785b5a2ca78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3282f6dd-ea0d-5250-b6a0-e1760944dcbc" :answer/id #uuid "3282f6dd-ea0d-5250-b6a0-e1760944dcbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{26}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b4cc4c19-d62f-5fe8-890e-23b350c71bdb" :question/id #uuid "b4cc4c19-d62f-5fe8-890e-23b350c71bdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-85663" :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{2}{3}(x-1)^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [1,4].$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}(x-1)^{3/2},$ $a=1,$ and $b=4.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(x-1)^{1/2}=\\sqrt{x-1}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\sqrt{x-1})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+x-1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\sqrt{x}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}]|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({4}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2(8-1)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9f3c91bd-b004-5988-9785-3182aa9872f4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9f3c91bd-b004-5988-9785-3182aa9872f4" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f3c91bd-b004-5988-9785-3182aa9872f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct 